    <string name="private_dns_warning">Private DNS is set to %1$s, so lookups go straight there and the firewall never sees them. Tap to fix.</string>
    <string name="private_dns_managed">Your Private DNS setting (%1$s) is paused while the firewall runs, so every lookup can be filtered. It comes back when you turn the firewall off.</string>
    <string name="private_dns_unknown_host">a fixed provider</string>
    <string name="private_dns_title">Private DNS is in the way</string>
    <string name="private_dns_fix_body">Android sends every lookup straight to %1$s over its own encrypted channel, so the firewall cannot filter any of them.\n\nThe firewall can switch Private DNS to Automatic while it runs and put your setting back the moment you turn it off. Your lookups stay encrypted: DNS over HTTPS stands in for it, with the same provider where it can.</string>
    <string name="private_dns_manual_body">Android sends every lookup straight to %1$s over its own encrypted channel, so the firewall cannot filter any of them.\n\nSet Private DNS to Automatic or Off under Network and internet, then turn on DNS over HTTPS here to keep lookups encrypted.\n\nOr let the firewall do this for you every time it runs, and put your setting back when it stops. Connect the phone to a computer with USB debugging on and run this once:\n\n%2$s</string>
